.TH FFIND 1 "April 2026" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ffind \- Recursively aggregate and copy files by extension or preset
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ffind
[ \-i \fIindir\fR ] [ \-o \fIoutdir\fR ] [ \-f \fIext1,ext2\fR | \-p \fIpreset\fR ] [ \-d ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ffind
recursively searches \fIindir\fR for files matching specified extensions and copies them to \fIoutdir\fR. Defaults to flat structure with collision numbering.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i " " \fIindir\fR
Target input directory.
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIoutdir\fR
Target output directory.
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIext1,ext2\fR
Comma-separated list of extensions.
.TP
.BR \-p " " \fIpreset\fR
Pre-defined extension groupings (zip, image, video, audio, txt).
.TP
.BR \-d
Replicate input directory tree structure in output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-help
Invoke runtime help block.
